 Abstract
-This study proposes an interactive psychological analysis system that interprets non-verbal emotional expression thr
-ough drawings and provides empathetic feedback. The proposed system detects key objects in drawings using YOLOv
-8 and generates counseling feedback through GPT-4o-mini by combining object detection success information with use
-r input. The object detection model was trained on a synthetic dataset of 33 classes and 330,000 images, achieving a 
-single-object mAP50 of approximately 0.92. The system also integrates a PDF report function for automatically docu
-menting counseling content, demonstrating the feasibility of digital psychological analysis and art therapy support.
-Key words
+This study proposes an interactive psychological analysis system that analyzes non-verbal emotional expression 
+through drawings and provides empathetic counseling feedback. The proposed system receives users’ drawings and 
+counseling input through a Gradio-based interface and detects key objects in the drawings using YOLOv8. The 
+detection result is summarized as detection success or failure and provided to GPT-4o-mini together with the user’s 
+emotional and situational input to generate empathetic counseling feedback. The object detection model was trained on 
+330,000 synthetic images across 33 classes, achieving approximately 0.92 mAP50 and 0.78 mAP50-95 on the training 
+data. The system also integrates automatic PDF report generation to support the documentation of analysis and 
+counseling results.
+Keywords
 generative AI, art therapy, emotional expression, counseling feedback, YOLOv8, GPT-4o-mini
 
